1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,330
同样一桌饭，同样的热量，
Same meals, same calories on the plate,

2
00:00:02,330 --> 00:00:04,480
有人一天多吃了五百大卡。
and people ate 500 extra calories a day.

3
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:07,590
今天的微博热搜：原来吃得差才会胖。
Today on Weibo's hot list: 'eating badly is what makes you fat.'

4
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:09,170
热度三千三百万。
33 million in heat.

5
00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:11,600
说法是：牛肉鸡蛋不是元凶，
The claim: beef and eggs aren't the culprits.

6
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:13,030
蛋糕奶茶才是。
Cake and milk tea are.

7
00:00:13,030 --> 00:00:15,360
今天的问题：一样多的热量，
Today's question: with the same calories,

8
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:17,620
为什么吃得“差”就会胖？
why does eating 'badly' make you fatter?

9
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:18,680
先认识小胃。
Meet Tummy.

10
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:21,280
它每天只问一句话：吃饱了吗？
It asks one thing all day: am I full yet?

11
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:24,980
二零一九年，美国国立卫生研究院做了一个实验。
In 2019, the US National Institutes of Health ran an experiment.

12
00:00:24,980 --> 00:00:27,960
二十个人，住进医院，整整四个星期。
Twenty people lived in a hospital for four weeks.

13
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:29,580
两周吃超加工食品，
Two weeks of ultra-processed food,

14
00:00:29,580 --> 00:00:31,870
两周吃少加工的天然食物。
two weeks of minimally processed food.

15
00:00:31,870 --> 00:00:35,800
关键是：两种饭端上来的热量、糖、脂肪、纤维，
The key: both diets served the same calories, sugar, fat and fiber.

16
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:36,820
全都一样。
Exactly matched.

17
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:39,270
想吃多少吃多少，没人逼。
Eat as much as you like. Nobody's forcing anyone.

18
00:00:39,270 --> 00:00:43,410
结果：超加工那两周，每人每天多吃了大约五百大卡。
Result: on ultra-processed food, people ate about 500 calories more per day.

19
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:44,900
差不多两碗米饭。
Roughly two bowls of rice.

20
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:47,570
两周下来，平均胖了将近一公斤。
In two weeks they gained almost a kilo on average.

21
00:00:47,570 --> 00:00:50,720
换成天然食物，又瘦了差不多那么多。
On the natural diet, they lost about the same.

22
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:54,100
反转一：大家给两种饭打分，一样好吃。
Twist one: people rated both diets equally tasty.

23
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:56,280
不是因为更香，才多吃。
It wasn't about flavor.

24
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:57,930
那多出来的五百大卡，
So where did those extra 500 calories

25
00:00:57,930 --> 00:00:59,370
到底是从哪来的？
come from?

26
00:00:59,370 --> 00:01:01,060
线索一：吃得更快。
Clue one: people ate faster.

27
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:04,550
超加工食品又软又好嚼，几口就下去了。
Soft, easy-to-chew food goes down in a few bites.

28
00:01:04,550 --> 00:01:07,630
而“吃饱了”的信号，从肠子传到大脑，
And the 'I'm full' signal takes time

29
00:01:07,630 --> 00:01:09,120
要花上一段时间。
to travel from the gut to the brain.

30
00:01:09,120 --> 00:01:12,140
就像外卖小哥送一张“够了”的纸条。
It's like a courier delivering a note that says 'enough.'

31
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:15,470
你吃得太快，纸条还没到，饭已经光了。
Eat too fast, and the plate is empty before the note arrives.

32
00:01:15,470 --> 00:01:17,130
线索二：热量密度。
Clue two: energy density.

33
00:01:17,130 --> 00:01:20,770
同样一口，超加工食品塞进去的热量更多。
Each bite of processed food packs in more calories.

34
00:01:20,770 --> 00:01:23,600
一块蛋糕和一盘青菜，个头差不多，
A slice of cake and a plate of greens look about the same size,

35
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:25,310
热量估计能差十倍。
but the calories can differ roughly tenfold.

36
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:28,390
而胃觉得饱，很大一部分是靠被撑开。
And a stomach feels full largely by being stretched.

37
00:01:28,390 --> 00:01:29,960
它不太会数热量。
It's bad at counting calories.

38
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:32,390
反转二：吃天然食物的那两周，
Twist two: on the natural diet,

39
00:01:32,390 --> 00:01:35,810
让人饱的激素升高了，让人饿的激素降了。
a fullness hormone went up and a hunger hormone went down.

40
00:01:35,810 --> 00:01:37,820
也就是说，吃天然食物，
In other words, on real food,

41
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:39,600
身体自己会踩刹车。
the body hits its own brakes.

42
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:43,390
反转三：“吃得差”说的不是吃得少，也不是穷，
Twist three: 'eating badly' isn't about eating little, or being poor.

43
00:01:43,390 --> 00:01:46,100
而是食物被加工得太“省事”了。
It's food processed to be too effortless.

44
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:48,420
工厂把嚼、剥、消化的活儿，
The factory has already done the chewing, peeling and breaking down

45
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:49,970
提前帮你干完了。
for you.

46
00:01:49,970 --> 00:01:51,420
对你的牙是省事了，
Easy on your teeth.

47
00:01:51,420 --> 00:01:53,320
对你的腰可就不省事了。
Not so easy on your waistline.

48
00:01:53,320 --> 00:01:55,350
奶茶为什么喝了不觉得饱？
Why doesn't milk tea fill you up?

49
00:01:55,350 --> 00:01:59,200
不少研究认为，喝下去的热量，大脑最容易漏算。
Many studies suggest the brain undercounts calories you drink.

50
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:02,280
那牛肉鸡蛋呢？蛋白质让人饱得更久，
And beef and eggs? Protein keeps you full longer,

51
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:04,580
同样的热量，更难吃过头。
so the same calories are harder to overeat.

52
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:07,320
所以热搜那句话，大方向是对的：
So the hot take is roughly right:

53
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:10,920
胖不胖，不只看吃多少，还看吃的是什么。
it's not only how much you eat, but what kind.

54
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:13,330
但别把它理解成“蛋糕有毒”。
But it doesn't mean cake is poison.

55
00:02:13,330 --> 00:02:14,660
热量还是热量。
A calorie is still a calorie.

56
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:16,270
只不过超加工食品，
Ultra-processed food just makes it

57
00:02:16,270 --> 00:02:18,000
让人特别容易多吃。
really easy to eat more.

58
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,810
友情提示：这只是一项二十个人、四周的小实验，
Friendly fine print: this was a small study, 20 people, four weeks.

59
00:02:21,810 --> 00:02:24,870
结论还要更多研究，每个人也不一样。
More research is needed, and everyone's different.

60
00:02:24,870 --> 00:02:26,870
身体有问题，听医生的，
For health questions, listen to your doctor,

61
00:02:26,870 --> 00:02:29,720
别听热搜的，也别听一块白板的。
not a hot list, and not a whiteboard.

62
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:32,110
最后送一个小建议：吃慢一点，
One last tip: eat a little slower,

63
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:34,970
让“够了”的纸条，追上你的筷子。
so the 'enough' note can catch up with your chopsticks.

64
00:02:34,970 --> 00:02:36,800
小胃说：我不是不饱，
Tummy says: I'm not never full.

65
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:38,440
我只是消息慢。
My messages are just slow.

